{"alias":"/learning/earlychildhood/first10/resources","title":"Resources for First 10 Schools and Communities ","changed":"2026-04-06T23:14:50+00:00","before":"<p><em>There are a variety of approaches for designing and developing First 10 Communities. The links below provide access to well-researched designs, all of which incorporate several key principles — public schools serve a central role; attention is paid to aligning learning across the birth to grade 5 spans; and children and families are connected to wrap-around services that enhance the quality of learning and care.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>First 10 Community Schools</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://nationalp-3center.org/\">Bridging ECE and PreK-12 Systems</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.communityschools.org/\">Coalition for Community Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.newamerica.org/education-policy/edcentral/first-10-schools-and-communities-helping-all-young-children-grow-and-thrive/\">First 10 Schools and Communities: Helping All Young Children Grow and Thrive</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"http://ceelo.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/CommunitySchoolsEarlyChildhood_Kappan_Jacobson.pdf\">Community Schools and Early Childhood Education</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/20-A/title20-Asec9922.html\">Maine Community Schools Statute</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Multi-Tiered Systems of Support (MTSS)</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.bc.edu/content/bc-web/schools/lynch-school/sites/coss.html\">The Center for Optimized Student Supports</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.edweek.org/education/how-schools-districts-and-communities-are-joining-forces-to-bolster-early-learning/2019/06\">How Schools, Districts, and Communities Are Joining Forces to Bolster Early Learning</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Alignment</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/2022-01/First%2010%20Draft%20of%20Alignment%20Guidebook%20Components.9-15-21.pdf\">Alignment Guidebook</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://learnwithmoose.maine.gov/module/1344/early-learning-foundational-skills-module-parents-and-caregivers/overview\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">MOOSE Foundational Skills Progression</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.cambridgema.gov/News/2015/11/~/media/F8450DA771B342529B5FF721684CAF21.ashx\">Starting Early: Addressing the Achievement Gap</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://learnwithmoose.maine.gov/\">Learn with MOOSE!</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://earlylearningnetwork.unl.edu/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/MDRC-Alignment-Policy-Brief-2019.pdf\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Pre-K to Grade 3 Alignment</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Literacy Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://lincs.ed.gov/publications/pdf/PRFbooklet.pdf\">Put Reading First – Helping Your Child Learn to Read (2006)</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"http://www.famlit.org/\">National Center for Family Literacy</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Nutrition Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/nutrition/programs\">Maine DOE - Child Nutrition</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/cacfplanding\">Child and Adult Care Food Program (CACFP)</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.foodpantries.org/\">Find Food Pantries</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.fns.usda.gov/meals4kids\">Free Summer Meals 4 Kids - 18 and Younger</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.211.org/get-help/food-programs-food-benefits\">Maine 211 - Food Programs &amp; Benefits</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","after":"<div class=\"doe-hero\">\n<p class=\"doe-eyebrow\">First 10: Schools and Communities in Maine</p>\n<p class=\"doe-lead\"><em>There are a variety of approaches for designing and developing First 10 Communities. The links below provide access to well-researched designs, all of which incorporate several key principles — public schools serve a central role; attention is paid to aligning learning across the birth to grade 5 spans; and children and families are connected to wrap-around services that enhance the quality of learning and care.</em></p>\n\n</div>\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\